  "is_sufficient": false,
  "knowledge_gaps": [
    "The experiment changes the original comparison: a gated recent-history model appears inside the common menu, but there is no dedicated budget-matched gated-baseline arm. This tests search ordering more directly than the starting hypothesis.",
    "Equal total GPU budgets and identical validation opportunities may conflict because diagnostic costs and intervention runtimes differ. If every arm completes the same configurations with fixed seeds, ordering alone should not change the selected maximum. Specify budget cutoffs, incomplete-trial handling, and the primary comparison.",
    "The gated residual and harder-negative mixture lack reproducible equations and settings: causal window, gate inputs and initialization, normalization, mixture weights, transition smoothing, negative exclusions, and sparse-transition fallback.",
    "Diagnostic thresholds, action mappings, conflict resolution, and abstention rules remain unspecified. Detecting artificial faults does not establish which training intervention will improve validation HR@10.",
    "Shuffling recommendations across only four categories can preserve assignments or exchange identical recommendations. Repeated searches need specified search-order seeds while retaining training seed 42; repeated deterministic training runs do not provide independent evidence.",
    "Originality 5/10 is plausible for the integrated protocol, but potential 8/10 and difficulty 5/10 are provisional. No demonstrated diagnostic-to-gain relationship or measured trial runtime supports those assessments. Five-user panels and repeatedly inspected validation outcomes also create adaptation risks."
  ],
  "follow_up_queries": [
    {
      "reason": "Clarify a comparison that isolates guidance value while accounting for diagnostic overhead, variable trial durations, and adaptive validation selection.",
      "query": "What established methods evaluate diagnostic-guided hyperparameter search against random search and a fixed strong baseline under equal total GPU-time budgets? Focus on best-so-far performance versus cumulative cost, incomplete-trial censoring, repeated search-order seeds with fixed training seeds, and selection bias from reusing validation outcomes."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Find concrete implementation precedents and stronger alternatives before fixing the intervention menu or assigning implementation difficulty.",
      "query": "For SASRec sequential recommendation, what published methods combine a causal recent-item embedding residual with a learned sigmoid gate, and what methods mix uniform negatives with training-transition hard negatives? Seek equations, gate initialization, normalization, sampling probabilities, false-negative handling, sparse-transition fallbacks, and ablations against simple recent-history baselines."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Assess whether fault calibration can support intervention selection and how to construct a meaningful placebo with only four dataset routes.",
      "query": "What research validates model diagnostics as predictors of subsequent intervention gains, beyond mutation-test fault detection? Seek prospective diagnostic-to-action policies, calibration without outcome leakage, abstention, and shuffled-guidance or permutation controls when there are few tasks and repeated action recommendations."
    }
  ]
}
